    "notes": "Building a resilient production environment starts with strong architectural foundations. Our first pillar is a truly comprehensive observability stack. For Docker, this means not just application logs, but also host-level metrics, Docker daemon health, and container-specific resource usage. We must also design for resilience from the ground up, particularly distinguishing between stateless and stateful workloads and ensuring data integrity and recoverability for the latter. Understanding the internal workings of Docker at runtime is crucial, so we'll discuss how to systematically gather diagnostic data. Finally, for complex microservice architectures, a service mesh becomes an invaluable tool for adding sophisticated control and visibility over container-to-container communication, enhancing both security and operational insights."
