    "takeaway": "Effective SRE for Docker involves proactive, intelligent alerting, a well-defined incident response framework, a culture of continuous learning from failures, and mastery of advanced diagnostic tools.",
    "notes": "This slide is the core of our discussion today – putting SRE into practice. It starts with intelligence: crafting custom Prometheus alerts that are truly actionable and tied to our SLOs, not just noisy thresholds. When an alert fires, we need a clear, pre-defined path to resolution, which is where structured runbooks come in. Post-incident, a blameless Root Cause Analysis (RCA) is vital to learn and prevent recurrence. This continuous feedback loop is what makes SRE powerful. Finally, when facing complex issues, we need to go beyond basic `docker logs` and leverage advanced Linux troubleshooting tools, sometimes even from within the container itself, to pinpoint and resolve deep-seated problems."
